    "lawCode": "Amd §19-508, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "New York City Administrative Code",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2379A\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in\nrelation to requiring certain for-hire vehicles to install and maintain\nan interior rear-facing video camera\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation requires certain for-hire vehicles to install and main-\ntain an interior rear-facing video camera to bring up-to-date current\nlaw while also adapting to new technology. It would also allow for the\nuse of front facing cameras as long as the minimum requirements are met.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill reletters subdivision c of section 19-508 of the\nadministrative code of the city of New York to subdivision d and adds a\nnew subdivision c to require for-hire vehicles with a seating capacity\nof six passengers or less that are dispatched by a livery base station,\nother than high-volume for-hire services, to install and maintain an\ninterior rear-facing video camera. Front-facing cameras are also allowed\nso long as they comply with the provisions below. Such video camera\nshall be recording at all times the vehicle is being operated for the\npurpose of for-hire transportation, and at minimum shall:\n\n(i) record anyone who enters and exits said vehicle\n\n(ii) store a minimum of the most recent 60 hours of operation and\n\n(iii) have the ability to transmit data or otherwise provide access to\nlocal law enforcement and the local regulatory authority\n\nSection 2 of the bill sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs it stands, current rear facing cameras requirements under 35 RCNY\n59C-01 are outdated and require a court order to access footage. This\nstatewide bill would allow competing providers to sell advanced and\nefficient rear facing cameras at an affordable rate. This bill would\nexempt black cars, limos, and luxury limos from these new requirements.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22: S.186 - Referred to Transportation\n\n2019-20: S.6147A - Referred to Transportation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
